  "transcript": "A new training trend is changing the way young professionals learn about leadership. Junior workers at several large companies are now invited to sit in on meetings with senior managers and observe how big decisions are made. The juniors take notes and ask questions afterwards rather than during the meeting. The companies say the practice has helped younger employees understand the bigger picture much faster. They have also reported stronger team relationships.",
